How strong do archon pets actually get?  I ask because I have my first
promising monk fresh out of Vlad's tower.  On the first level, I enter
and see a purple A.  This causes me some consternation until I
remember I'm playing a lawful monk.  This should be a peaceful archon.
 I am concerned a bit because I'm only XL 15, purposely keeping my XL
low to minimize the monster level.  I didn't think archons could even
be created until I was a few levels higher.

Anyway, I sidle up to the archon, cast charm monster a few times. 
After the fifth try (which I told myself would be my last, due to food
and Pw issues), "The invisible archon wields a long sword named
Sunsword."  Sure enough, I have a new pet.  He's already taken out
Vlad in one round.  My pet winged gargoyle met his end at the breath
of a black dragon; I left my pet vampire lord in Vlad's tower.  I
didn't really feel like I needed them any more.

How good of a pet is this really?  I mean, I fear archons more than
most monsters... I haven't even seen an archon in a good many games. 
They must be pretty buff, since many pacifists ascend with an archon
or two in tow...

